\f1\b \cf0 Early notes from 23 July 2026
\f0\b0 \
\
Double Slit:\
- 2 setups\
- PMT has a light sensor that triggers an alarm (even if PMT is off)\
- Diode in front is used for \'93classical\'94 measurement (measure a voltage); opening the tube exposes the PMT to do the \'93single photons\'94 experiment that is not really a single photons experiment \
- PMT connects to laptop and gives a value that is a count per second\
- two light sources (laser and bulb)\
- single slit and double slit are magnetic\'97have to mounted relatively centered and upright\
- there is another single slit near the detector; they make measurements as a function of position of the final slit in order to sample the illumination function\
- use the laser for the \'93classical\'94 measurement, bulb for \'93single photon\'94\
- pull up the bulb to be in line with the laser; don\'92t touch the slits after that point\
- start PMT when the final slit is at the maximum; should be getting a a couple thousand counts\
- given the length of the tube and the speed of light, can show there is ~1 photon in the tub at a time, hence \'93single photon\'94\
- 2nd setup (in the back room) you move the laser out of the beam of the lightbulb instead of moving the bulb in front of the laser\
\

